# One domain per vendor service, with the transition init needs to leave u:r:init:s0.
#
# Nothing here is permissive. Getting to that took two steps and the first one is the reason
# the second was possible at all. Global permissive is not a substitute for a domain: a
# service started with no transition runs AS init, so servicemanager registration and lookup
# misbehave and keystore2 cannot reach keymint. So each service got its own domain and was
# marked permissive while its rules were written.
#
# The rules then turned out to be mostly present already. Declared as a bare type plus
# init_daemon_domain, a domain has an identity but none of the client or server attributes
# the HAL framework keys its rules on, so AOSP's own rules and the ones recovered from stock
# both sat inert. hal_clients.te declares those relationships, and with them the permissive
# lines became unnecessary rather than being replaced by hand-written rules.

type ambience_hub_default, domain;
init_daemon_domain(ambience_hub_default)

type aocd, domain;
init_daemon_domain(aocd)

