# The widevine DRM HAL. Its binary was labelled but no domain was declared, so init had
# nowhere to transition into and fell back to execute_no_trans, which AOSP forbids: under
# enforcing the service does not start, and under permissive it runs as init. Stock declares
# both halves. Its rules come from the stock policy like the rest, and were being skipped
# while the domain did not exist.
#
# hal_server_domain supplies the three attributes stock carries beyond domain, and they are
# what the HAL actually runs on: the rules it needs are AOSP's, written against hal_drm_server
# rather than against this domain, so declaring the type alone left them inert. Without them
# it cannot reach servicemanager, addService returns -129, and it aborts on its own CHECK
# every five seconds. Stock's own vendor policy adds only four rules on top of these.
type hal_drm_widevine, domain;
hal_server_domain(hal_drm_widevine, hal_drm)
init_daemon_domain(hal_drm_widevine)
